[{:db/id "q-335058/field-1/0952ea59fa515cef66d9cbfbae0848f88c900b639706872192613c4f7410e2b4" :answer/id #uuid "991c997c-dec1-517a-ac1c-8fd8a12c4e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335058/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "438bcf43-10c6-5f9b-abc7-d7ed9ba2c72c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335058/field-1/0952ea59fa515cef66d9cbfbae0848f88c900b639706872192613c4f7410e2b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-335058/field-1/0952ea59fa515cef66d9cbfbae0848f88c900b639706872192613c4f7410e2b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335058" :question/id #uuid "6d8836cc-59e2-5008-b730-102c5a1987fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-335058" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4y(t)-4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335058/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335085/field-1/a11ac582ee8c8174b3a65ee992ecb257b1b3f11a139f25fa2a469a2fd6b4905e" :answer/id #uuid "18a18302-cbe3-5f13-a21e-05aa3bd72476" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335085/field-1/45dfac0fd167744b149e7e3e8902f78ea0f844baf7ffaae5e33fabfc6f444c95" :answer/id #uuid "bb9403db-54d2-5df6-8db1-299254e21a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{5t}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335085/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a69232a6-2281-5045-a5f1-fa52926c037d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335085/field-1/a11ac582ee8c8174b3a65ee992ecb257b1b3f11a139f25fa2a469a2fd6b4905e" :answer-field/choices ["q-335085/field-1/a11ac582ee8c8174b3a65ee992ecb257b1b3f11a139f25fa2a469a2fd6b4905e" "q-335085/field-1/45dfac0fd167744b149e7e3e8902f78ea0f844baf7ffaae5e33fabfc6f444c95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335085" :question/id #uuid "f8bec585-bc4b-5d00-82b9-c3eb8cbec5b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335085" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335085/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335085"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" :answer/id #uuid "257635f6-3b39-5ff1-b19f-c69286ac6380" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-1/90f9b3aa8bf944a7feca6948bc9b4f8b714976f2a4f40ee10776f871c3970cd2" :answer/id #uuid "cc0206d5-347c-5656-ac8c-14b1f8ae2307" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-1/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" :answer/id #uuid "e6049fdc-9767-5a2c-987e-1e2df78f6c45" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" :answer/id #uuid "8bf099f7-0e6b-5e5c-abbf-d9ad30c380b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8309503-c205-5bc5-a9c3-0c4a27dc5d42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335396/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" :answer-field/choices ["q-335396/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" "q-335396/field-1/90f9b3aa8bf944a7feca6948bc9b4f8b714976f2a4f40ee10776f871c3970cd2" "q-335396/field-1/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" "q-335396/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-2/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" :answer/id #uuid "ee6752c1-0ac9-5ff7-9386-7cf8cf0a7845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-2/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer/id #uuid "7fcedd0c-2fe1-5759-bc3f-047489fd3a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-2/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" :answer/id #uuid "3c10454b-6dfe-5bee-9c61-bfe26975fb72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2dbe461-3022-5ae8-ae95-cabdfed6f0df" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335396/field-2/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335396/field-2/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" "q-335396/field-2/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" "q-335396/field-2/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/val