pe :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-4/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" :answer/id #uuid "c308029d-b095-5fa7-a04d-16870a5c7d20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-4/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" :answer/id #uuid "5691069b-e2e3-5a2d-90ce-6ccf5fe101f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8b0e80-0b30-5838-b3dd-12a82beecd18" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335396/field-4/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" :answer-field/choices ["q-335396/field-4/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" "q-335396/field-4/f749d373f36b73b0de831ea8ea8419ce510169b7fc94f0c58ed2ac4aa2800881" "q-335396/field-4/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" "q-335396/field-4/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335396" :question/id #uuid "6a7bc535-4874-57d4-b853-7c25f0a7de43" :question/math-academy-id "q-335396" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335396/field-1" "q-335396/field-2" "q-335396/field-3" "q-335396/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335422/field-1/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279